# Vercel serves the deployment root as static files. This repo stays private until
# submission on 13 Sep, so ship only what the page actually fetches: app/, the
# replay CSV it reads, and the README. Everything else — the contracts, the tests,
# the scripts, the keeper — is the edge, and it goes public on our schedule, not
# because a static host happened to serve it.
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash. Without it these are
# gitignore patterns that match at any depth, and `src/` silently deletes
# `app/src/` too — which is exactly what happened on the first deploy: the page
# shipped, every module 404'd, and it hung on "connecting to HyperEVM…".
/src/
/test/
/script/
/keeper/
/subgraph/
/lib/
/out/
/cache/
/broadcast/
/node_modules/
/tape/
/.github/
/foundry.toml
/remappings.txt
/package.json
/yarn.lock
